Z||000009||HAGS||02-10-2001||08:57 AM||||My brother is being killed by Porches over in Germany as we speak, he never mentioned having to change out any bulbs.  He is military so didnt have to pay(atleast not as much as a civilian if he did) to bring the car over.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Tina||02-10-2001||09:21 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by HAGS:<BR><B>My brother is being killed by Porches over in Germany as we speak, he never mentioned having to change out any bulbs.  He is military so didnt have to pay(atleast not as much as a civilian if he did) to bring the car over.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Porches, hahaha<BR>Didn't know they could move.<BR>No offense man, but this was a classic typo.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>As for the U.S.military vehicles.<BR>The standards do not apply to them, none of them do.<BR>Don't quote me on this,but I  believe they can't even be pulled over by the local law.<BR>Or at least MP's must be present a the time.<BR>German plates totally different story.<BR>There bi-yeary complete check is a nightmare.<BR>(Trust me,I know)<BR>They actually go underneath with a hammer and <BR>attack everything. You got rust,you don't pass. Myself,had a hole in front fender.<BR>Size of penny. NO PASS. Went back (new fender) only to leave a drop of oil behind.NO PASS AGAIN.<BR>It get irritating, but look at the flipside.<BR>With no Speedlimit. The last thing I want to have is some decrepid "bucket" shedding is <BR>pieces in front of me,while doing 200mph.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tina.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000011||qwikgta||02-12-2001||09:15 PM||||I just returned from 2 years in Bahrain (a small island in "the gulf") anyway, there were at least 3 Fiero's over there.  Two coupes and a GT, (84, 87, 87) I tryed to get the GT from the owner but he would not sell.  Parts were a big prob too, there was none.  Lots of "rice" and German rides.  Oh yea, the military could get pulled over - over there.<P>Rob<P>------------------<BR>QWIKGTA<BR>88 T-Top coupe<BR>http://robsfieroproject.homestead.com/index.html||||reg||1
